{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKEbWRBiPtEh1j33K6B8Ac","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tr\"\"\"errorlist_check - the cycle-start LabVIEW Error List check (user decision 5, 2026-09-24):\n2\t\"사이클 시작하기 전에 LabVIEW 컴파일 에러 창은 반드시 확인해야할듯. GUI로 에러 내용 확인하고 각 에러 더블클릭하면 에러\n3\t위치로 이동해서 보여주거든. (블락 다이어그램 켜진 상태에서)\".\n4\t\n5\tWHAT ALREADY EXISTS (checked first): `tools/lv_errorlist.py` reads every Error List row by capture+OCR, count-checked\n6\tagainst the window's own \"N errors and warnings\" (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:313; test tools/bench/diag_errorlist_v0.py).\n7\tThis file REUSES it unchanged except for one optional per-item hook (`on_item`), and adds: a byte-identical SCRATCH copy\n8\t(the bed itself is never opened), Ctrl+E so the block diagram is up, a double-click per item with a capture of the\n9\tblock diagram before/after, a zero-item path for a runnable VI, the expected-errors comparison, and the cleanup proofs.\n10\tThe selected object's UID is NOT read: `TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]` 0x6349400 exists (NI API ref) but the fleet\n11\thas no op that reads it (`grep \"Selection\" tools/gscript.py` -> 0), and branching `Open VI Reference.vi reference`\n12\tinto a VI-class property node is a MEASURED failure (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:666). Recorded per item as uid=None.\n13\t\n14\tPREDICTION CONTRACT: Ctrl+E opens '<scratch> Block Diagram'; Ctrl+L opens a new 'Error list' window; items read ==\n15\tthe window's own N (0 for a runnable VI); each double-click fronts the block diagram and changes its capture; the\n16\tError List is closed with Esc; the scratch is closed and deleted; the bed md5 is unchanged; no VI is run or saved.\n17\tEvery GUI act goes through lv_gui.ps1 with -Exception Approved -Evidence EVID (logged to tools/gui_actions.log).\n18\t\n19\t  py tools/errorlist_check.py [--vi <bed.vi>] [--expected <file.json>]      rc 0 OK / 1 MISMATCH / 2 FAIL\n20\t  expected file: {\"expected\": [{\"match\": \"<substring of the row text>\", \"count\": n}, ...]}  (default: none = [])\n21\tLast stdout line: `ERRORLIST-VERDICT: OK|MISMATCH|FAIL <json path>`.\n22\t\"\"\"\n23\timport argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys, time\n24\t\n25\tHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n26\tROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)\n27\tsys.path.insert(0, HERE)\n28\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\"))\n29\t# LAZY LabVIEW IMPORTS (card 81-1, 2026-09-25): the offline re-verdict (`find_reusable` / `reverdict`, used by\n30\t# cycle_runner.errorlist_hook when the bed md5 is unchanged) must import nothing LabVIEW-side, so gscript /\n31\t# lv_errorlist / bench_prep are bound only by `_lv_imports()`, which main() calls first. Same modules, same order.\n32\tg = E = labview_handles = None\n33\tCLAUDEDEV = r\"C:\\Program Files\\National Instruments\\LabVIEW 2026\\user.lib\\claudeDev\"   # == gscript.CLAUDEDEV\n34\t\n35\tEVID = \"user 2026-09-24 error-list check at cycle start\"\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tdef _lv_imports():\n39\t    global g, E, labview_handles\n40\t    if g is None:\n41\t        import gscript as _g\n42\t        import lv_errorlist as _E\n43\t        from bench_prep import labview_handles as _lh\n44\t        g, E, labview_handles = _g, _E, _lh\n45\t        E.EVIDENCE = EVID\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tBENCH = os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\")\n49\t# 2026-09-24 card chat-C2: external search (WebSearch, \"LabVIEW scripting read selected objects block diagram\n50\t# Selection List\") found no route other than a VI Server property node on TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]; the\n51\t# ActiveX VirtualInstrument interface has no diagram access (toolkit-capabilities.md:666), and building an op VI is\n52\t# outside a labview=read card. So the uid is not read here; the after-capture of the diagram is the record.\n53\tUID_ROUTE = \"none: needs a Selection List[] 6349400 op (unbuilt; card labview=read) - screenshot recorded\"\n54\tCOUNT_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s*errors?\\s*and\\s*warnings?\", re.I)\n55\t\n56\t\n57\tdef md5(p):\n58\t    return hashlib.md5(open(p, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n59\t\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"535e9f41-c187-4540-86af-0d509cb572c3","uuid":"b23d12f0-2537-4f68-98e2-3128c29ab1e3","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:45:46.380Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"G:\\Codes\\LabVIEW_Codes\\MinLab\\zz_LabView VI\\AAA_UNIST\\2. Tracking\\V6_ParallelLoop\\tools\\errorlist_check.py","content":"r\"\"\"errorlist_check - the cycle-start LabVIEW Error List check (user decision 5, 2026-09-24):\n\"사이클 시작하기 전에 LabVIEW 컴파일 에러 창은 반드시 확인해야할듯. GUI로 에러 내용 확인하고 각 에러 더블클릭하면 에러\n위치로 이동해서 보여주거든. (블락 다이어그램 켜진 상태에서)\".\n\nWHAT ALREADY EXISTS (checked first): `tools/lv_errorlist.py` reads every Error List row by capture+OCR, count-checked\nagainst the window's own \"N errors and warnings\" (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:313; test tools/bench/diag_errorlist_v0.py).\nThis file REUSES it unchanged except for one optional per-item hook (`on_item`), and adds: a byte-identical SCRATCH copy\n(the bed itself is never opened), Ctrl+E so the block diagram is up, a double-click per item with a capture of the\nblock diagram before/after, a zero-item path for a runnable VI, the expected-errors comparison, and the cleanup proofs.\nThe selected object's UID is NOT read: `TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]` 0x6349400 exists (NI API ref) but the fleet\nhas no op that reads it (`grep \"Selection\" tools/gscript.py` -> 0), and branching `Open VI Reference.vi reference`\ninto a VI-class property node is a MEASURED failure (docs/toolkit-capabilities.md:666). Recorded per item as uid=None.\n\nPREDICTION CONTRACT: Ctrl+E opens '<scratch> Block Diagram'; Ctrl+L opens a new 'Error list' window; items read ==\nthe window's own N (0 for a runnable VI); each double-click fronts the block diagram and changes its capture; the\nError List is closed with Esc; the scratch is closed and deleted; the bed md5 is unchanged; no VI is run or saved.\nEvery GUI act goes through lv_gui.ps1 with -Exception Approved -Evidence EVID (logged to tools/gui_actions.log).\n\n  py tools/errorlist_check.py [--vi <bed.vi>] [--expected <file.json>]      rc 0 OK / 1 MISMATCH / 2 FAIL\n  expected file: {\"expected\": [{\"match\": \"<substring of the row text>\", \"count\": n}, ...]}  (default: none = [])\nLast stdout line: `ERRORLIST-VERDICT: OK|MISMATCH|FAIL <json path>`.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys, time\n\nHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\nROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)\nsys.path.insert(0, HERE)\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\"))\n# LAZY LabVIEW IMPORTS (card 81-1, 2026-09-25): the offline re-verdict (`find_reusable` / `reverdict`, used by\n# cycle_runner.errorlist_hook when the bed md5 is unchanged) must import nothing LabVIEW-side, so gscript /\n# lv_errorlist / bench_prep are bound only by `_lv_imports()`, which main() calls first. Same modules, same order.\ng = E = labview_handles = None\nCLAUDEDEV = r\"C:\\Program Files\\National Instruments\\LabVIEW 2026\\user.lib\\claudeDev\"   # == gscript.CLAUDEDEV\n\nEVID = \"user 2026-09-24 error-list check at cycle start\"\n\n\ndef _lv_imports():\n    global g, E, labview_handles\n    if g is None:\n        import gscript as _g\n        import lv_errorlist as _E\n        from bench_prep import labview_handles as _lh\n        g, E, labview_handles = _g, _E, _lh\n        E.EVIDENCE = EVID\n\n\nBENCH = os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\")\n# 2026-09-24 card chat-C2: external search (WebSearch, \"LabVIEW scripting read selected objects block diagram\n# Selection List\") found no route other than a VI Server property node on TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]; the\n# ActiveX VirtualInstrument interface has no diagram access (toolkit-capabilities.md:666), and building an op VI is\n# outside a labview=read card. So the uid is not read here; the after-capture of the diagram is the record.\nUID_ROUTE = \"none: needs a Selection List[] 6349400 op (unbuilt; card labview=read) - screenshot recorded\"\nCOUNT_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s*errors?\\s*and\\s*warnings?\", re.I)\n\n\ndef md5(p):\n    return hashlib.md5(open(p, \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()\n\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":768}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxNAyHNfksGM178bosK9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A5K15jLVbcgT5QBzdi5FuR","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"G:\\Codes\\LabVIEW_Codes\\MinLab\\zz_LabView VI\\AAA_UNIST\\2. Tracking\\V6_ParallelLoop\\tools\\errorlist_check.py","offset":310,"limit":180},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":108632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"535e9f41-c187-4540-86af-0d509cb572c3","uuid":"8f0b046a-15fd-4f0a-8d2f-abecff6f9ec6","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:45:47.158Z","request_id":"req_011CfxNAx9QyiFBbcxeMgyLm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01A5K15jLVbcgT5QBzdi5FuR":{"file_path":"G:\\Codes\\LabVIEW_Codes\\MinLab\\zz_LabView VI\\AAA_UNIST\\2. Tracking\\V6_ParallelLoop\\tools\\errorlist_check.py","offset":310,"limit":180}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5K15jLVbcgT5QBzdi5FuR","type":"tool_result","content":"310\t            if m:\n311\t                return int(m.group(1)), t, p\n312\t    return None, None, caps[-1] if caps else None\n313\t\n314\t\n315\tdef norm(s):\n316\t    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]\", \"\", (s or \"\").lower())\n317\t\n318\t\n319\t# card 127-2 (PD255(a) carry; review archive/peer/2026-10-01-c126-4-elocr.md:73): OCR reads 'SubVI' as 'subvl' and\n320\t# 'anything' as 'anvthing'. ADD-ONLY: norm() is unchanged (expected files store its keys); norm_ocr() is the alias-folded\n321\t# form, applied to BOTH sides only where a caller opts in (_hit's fallback, class_counts(ocr=True)).\n322\tOCR_ALIASES = ((\"vl\", \"vi\"), (\"v\", \"y\"))\n323\t\n324\t\n325\tdef ocr_fold(k):\n326\t    for a, b in OCR_ALIASES:\n327\t        k = k.replace(a, b)\n328\t    return k\n329\t\n330\t\n331\tdef norm_ocr(s):\n332\t    return ocr_fold(norm(s))\n333\t\n334\t\n335\t# EXPECTED ERRORS FROM THE PLAN (card chat-E2): a staged bed is broken BY DESIGN - its plan\n336\t# (tools/bench/plan_<stage>*.json, schema stageplan/1) declares `open_rows` [{node, term, why}] left for a later\n337\t# stage. Each open row licenses the Error List items LabVIEW raises for it, derived per node class from the plan's\n338\t# base graph (`base.path` objs[].class): a SubVI -> \"... '<term>' is not wired\" (only REQUIRED inputs are listed,\n339\t# so the licence is not required to appear); any other node -> one \"Contains unwired or bad terminal\"; and the\n340\t# half-wires an open row leaves -> the wire classes in WIRE_CLASSES. Their COUNT is not derivable from open_rows\n341\t# (one deleted sink can leave loose ends on several branches), so the wire licence is class-level and uncapped;\n342\t# the JSON records how many items it absorbed. Anything no licence covers is `extra` -> MISMATCH.\n343\tWIRE_CLASSES = (\"wirehaslooseends\", \"hasnosource\", \"outputlooptunneltoaninput\", \"twoterminalsofdifferenttypes\")\n344\t# REVERTED by docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md Pre-decided 195(b) (cycle 88): cycle 87's uncapped additions\n345\t# \"isnotconnectedtoanything\" and \"zerosources\" are removed - an uncapped class licence hides a real fault of the same\n346\t# wording (archive/peer/2026-09-26-c87-errorlist-extras.md:118). The L2-A1 bed's items are licensed instead by an\n347\t# explicit, exact-count file: tools/bench/errorlist_expected_D1_l2_a1_20260925_235224.json.\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tdef plan_for_bed(bed, bench=None):\n351\t    \"\"\"stage_d1_<s>.json whose `work` is this bed -> the stageplan plan_<s>*.json carrying open_rows.\"\"\"\n352\t    BENCH_ = bench or BENCH\n353\t    name = os.path.basename(bed).lower()\n354\t    for sp in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"stage_d1_*.json\"))):\n355\t        try:\n356\t            if os.path.basename(str(json.load(open(sp, encoding=\"utf-8\")).get(\"work\") or \"\")).lower() != name:\n357\t                continue\n358\t        except Exception:                                                          # noqa: BLE001\n359\t            continue\n360\t        stage = os.path.basename(sp)[len(\"stage_d1_\"):-len(\".json\")]\n361\t        # cycle-87 firefighter: a simulated stage (docs/stage-simulator-plan.md) keeps its finalized plan under\n362\t        # tools/bench/sim/<stage>/ (plan_<stage>.json, stageplan_<stage>.json), not in tools/bench/; without this\n363\t        # the L2-A1 bed derived 0 licences and every one of its 35 by-design items was `extra` (cycle 87 MISMATCH).\n364\t        cands = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"plan_%s*.json\" % stage)))\n365\t        cands += sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"sim\", stage, \"plan_%s*.json\" % stage)))\n366\t        cands += sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"sim\", stage, \"stageplan_%s*.json\" % stage)))\n367\t        for pp in cands:\n368\t            try:\n369\t                p = json.load(open(pp, encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n370\t            except Exception:                                                      # noqa: BLE001\n371\t                continue\n372\t            if p.get(\"schema\") == \"stageplan/1\" and \"open_rows\" in p:\n373\t                return sp, pp, p\n374\t    return None, None, None\n375\t\n376\t\n377\tdef derive_expected(plan):\n378\t    base = (plan.get(\"base\") or {}).get(\"path\")\n379\t    cls = {}\n380\t    if base and os.path.exists(os.path.join(ROOT, base)):\n381\t        for o in json.load(open(os.path.join(ROOT, base), encoding=\"utf-8\")).get(\"objs\") or []:\n382\t            cls[o.get(\"uid\")] = o.get(\"class\")\n383\t    rules, seen_nodes = [], set()\n384\t    for r in plan.get(\"open_rows\") or []:\n385\t        n, t = int(r[\"node\"]), r[\"term\"]\n386\t        c = cls.get(n)\n387\t        if c == \"SubVI\":\n388\t            rules.append({\"norm_all\": [norm(t), \"isnotwired\"], \"count\": 1, \"required\": False,\n389\t                          \"kind\": \"subvi_input_not_wired\", \"from\": [n, t, c]})\n390\t        elif n not in seen_nodes:\n391\t            rules.append({\"norm_all\": [\"containsunwiredorbadterminal\"], \"count\": 1, \"required\": False,\n392\t                          \"kind\": \"node_unwired\", \"from\": [n, t, c]})\n393\t        seen_nodes.add(n)\n394\t    if plan.get(\"open_rows\"):\n395\t        rules.append({\"norm_any\": list(WIRE_CLASSES), \"count\": None, \"required\": False,\n396\t                      \"kind\": \"wire_from_open_rows\", \"from\": \"all open rows\"})\n397\t    return rules\n398\t\n399\t\n400\tdef _hit(rule, txt):\n401\t    if \"match\" in rule:\n402\t        return rule[\"match\"].lower() in txt.lower()\n403\t    n = norm(txt)\n404\t    if \"norm_all\" in rule:\n405\t        if all(k in n for k in rule[\"norm_all\"]):\n406\t            return True\n407\t        n2 = ocr_fold(n)                                   # card 127-2: OCR-alias fallback (only adds matches)\n408\t        return all(ocr_fold(k) in n2 for k in rule[\"norm_all\"])\n409\t    if any(k in n for k in rule.get(\"norm_any\") or []):\n410\t        return True\n411\t    n2 = ocr_fold(n)\n412\t    return any(ocr_fold(k) in n2 for k in rule.get(\"norm_any\") or [])\n413\t\n414\t\n415\tdef compare(items, expected, derived=()):\n416\t    \"\"\"Explicit expected entries (file) are REQUIRED; plan-derived licences are not. Returns extra raws, missing\n417\t    explicit matches, and per-rule usage.\"\"\"\n418\t    left = [dict(e, count=int(e.get(\"count\", 1)), required=True, kind=\"explicit\") for e in expected]\n419\t    left += [dict(d) for d in derived]\n420\t    used = [0] * len(left)\n421\t    extra = []\n422\t    for it in items:\n423\t        txt = \"%s %s\" % (it.get(\"raw\") or \"\", it.get(\"detail\") or \"\")\n424\t        k = next((i for i, e in enumerate(left) if (e[\"count\"] is None or e[\"count\"] > 0) and _hit(e, txt)), None)\n425\t        if k is None:\n426\t            extra.append(it.get(\"raw\"))\n427\t            continue\n428\t        used[k] += 1\n429\t        it[\"licensed_by\"] = left[k][\"kind\"]\n430\t        if left[k][\"count\"] is not None:\n431\t            left[k][\"count\"] -= 1\n432\t    missing = [e.get(\"match\") for e in left if e[\"required\"] for _ in range(e[\"count\"])]\n433\t    usage = [{\"kind\": e[\"kind\"], \"from\": e.get(\"from\") or e.get(\"match\"), \"used\": u} for e, u in zip(left, used)]\n434\t    heads = license_headers(items)\n435\t    for pos in heads:                                   # remove exactly the licensed empty headers from `extra`\n436\t        extra.remove(items[pos].get(\"raw\"))\n437\t    usage.append({\"kind\": \"header_of_next\", \"from\": \"PD179(d): empty-raw tree header before a licensed item\",\n438\t                  \"used\": len(heads)})\n439\t    return extra, missing, usage\n440\t\n441\t\n442\t# TREE-HEADER ROWS (card 80-4, plan PD179(d), 2026-09-25): the Error List shows a subVI's required-input error as a\n443\t# tree - a header row whose OCR text can come back EMPTY, then the item row. cycle 80 read item 0 raw='' with the\n444\t# detail of item 1 (#5058 'Image In' is not wired, licensed by an open row) and called it extra. An empty-raw row is\n445\t# licensed ONLY when (a) the NEXT item is itself licensed and non-empty, and (b) the header's detail text (the error\n446\t# class description) equals that item's detail after norm(). It consumes no licence count. Anything else stays extra.\n447\t\n448\tdef license_headers(items):\n449\t    \"\"\"Mark `licensed_by = 'header-of <n>'` on qualifying empty-raw rows; return their positions in `items`.\"\"\"\n450\t    out = []\n451\t    for pos, it in enumerate(items):\n452\t        if it.get(\"licensed_by\") or norm(it.get(\"raw\")) or pos + 1 >= len(items):\n453\t            continue\n454\t        nxt = items[pos + 1]\n455\t        det = norm(it.get(\"detail\"))\n456\t        if not (nxt.get(\"licensed_by\") and not str(nxt[\"licensed_by\"]).startswith(\"header-of\")\n457\t                and norm(nxt.get(\"raw\")) and det and det == norm(nxt.get(\"detail\"))):\n458\t            continue\n459\t        it[\"licensed_by\"] = \"header-of %s\" % nxt.get(\"index\", pos + 1)\n460\t        out.append(pos)\n461\t    return out\n462\t\n463\t\n464\t# COUNT-ONLY SCRATCH READ (card chat-P2 item 3, user 2026-09-28 \"1~4번 적용\"): a stage that reads the Error List of a\n465\t# SCRATCH copy and then of the saved FINAL file paid two full reads (pool stage: scratch 664 s + final 665 s). The\n466\t# expensive part of a full read is the per-item double-click (make_on_item: two block-diagram captures + 1.5 s each).\n467\t# `--count-only --role scratch` walks the list WITHOUT the double-clicks (rows and details are still OCR'd, so every\n468\t# item's text and the per-class counts are read) and compares the per-class counts with the expected file; if they\n469\t# differ (any extra, any missing, or items != the window's own N) the FULL read runs at once on the same scratch,\n470\t# exactly as before. `--role final` (the default) ALWAYS gets the full read: --count-only is refused for it and said so.\n471\tdef class_counts(items, ocr=False):\n472\t    \"\"\"{norm(raw): n} over the read items - the per-class counts a count-only read is judged by. card 127-2: ocr=True\n473\t    keys by norm_ocr (OCR aliases folded, e.g. subvi/subvl one class); the default is unchanged.\"\"\"\n474\t    out = {}\n475\t    for it in items or []:\n476\t        k = norm_ocr(it.get(\"raw\")) if ocr else norm(it.get(\"raw\"))\n477\t        out[k] = out.get(k, 0) + 1\n478\t    return dict(sorted(out.items()))\n479\t\n480\t\n481\tdef count_only_differs(items, n_reported, expected, derived):\n482\t    \"\"\"(differs: bool, why: str) - a count-only read is accepted only when it matches the expectation exactly.\"\"\"\n483\t    import copy\n484\t    ex, mi, _u = compare(copy.deepcopy(items or []), expected, [dict(d) for d in derived])\n485\t    why = []\n486\t    if n_reported is None or len(items or []) != n_reported:\n487\t        why.append(\"items %s != window N %s\" % (len(items or []), n_reported))\n488\t    if ex:\n489\t        why.append(\"%d extra\" % len(ex))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"535e9f41-c187-4540-86af-0d509cb572c3","uuid":"0a7b99e4-abb6-4e3e-88dc-20fd84ee0044","timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:45:47.332Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"G:\\Codes\\LabVIEW_Codes\\MinLab\\zz_LabView VI\\AAA_UNIST\\2. Tracking\\V6_ParallelLoop\\tools\\errorlist_check.py","content":"            if m:\n                return int(m.group(1)), t, p\n    return None, None, caps[-1] if caps else None\n\n\ndef norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]\", \"\", (s or \"\").lower())\n\n\n# card 127-2 (PD255(a) carry; review archive/peer/2026-10-01-c126-4-elocr.md:73): OCR reads 'SubVI' as 'subvl' and\n# 'anything' as 'anvthing'. ADD-ONLY: norm() is unchanged (expected files store its keys); norm_ocr() is the alias-folded\n# form, applied to BOTH sides only where a caller opts in (_hit's fallback, class_counts(ocr=True)).\nOCR_ALIASES = ((\"vl\", \"vi\"), (\"v\", \"y\"))\n\n\ndef ocr_fold(k):\n    for a, b in OCR_ALIASES:\n        k = k.replace(a, b)\n    return k\n\n\ndef norm_ocr(s):\n    return ocr_fold(norm(s))\n\n\n# EXPECTED ERRORS FROM THE PLAN (card chat-E2): a staged bed is broken BY DESIGN - its plan\n# (tools/bench/plan_<stage>*.json, schema stageplan/1) declares `open_rows` [{node, term, why}] left for a later\n# stage. Each open row licenses the Error List items LabVIEW raises for it, derived per node class from the plan's\n# base graph (`base.path` objs[].class): a SubVI -> \"... '<term>' is not wired\" (only REQUIRED inputs are listed,\n# so the licence is not required to appear); any other node -> one \"Contains unwired or bad terminal\"; and the\n# half-wires an open row leaves -> the wire classes in WIRE_CLASSES. Their COUNT is not derivable from open_rows\n# (one deleted sink can leave loose ends on several branches), so the wire licence is class-level and uncapped;\n# the JSON records how many items it absorbed. Anything no licence covers is `extra` -> MISMATCH.\nWIRE_CLASSES = (\"wirehaslooseends\", \"hasnosource\", \"outputlooptunneltoaninput\", \"twoterminalsofdifferenttypes\")\n# REVERTED by docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md Pre-decided 195(b) (cycle 88): cycle 87's uncapped additions\n# \"isnotconnectedtoanything\" and \"zerosources\" are removed - an uncapped class licence hides a real fault of the same\n# wording (archive/peer/2026-09-26-c87-errorlist-extras.md:118). The L2-A1 bed's items are licensed instead by an\n# explicit, exact-count file: tools/bench/errorlist_expected_D1_l2_a1_20260925_235224.json.\n\n\ndef plan_for_bed(bed, bench=None):\n    \"\"\"stage_d1_<s>.json whose `work` is this bed -> the stageplan plan_<s>*.json carrying open_rows.\"\"\"\n    BENCH_ = bench or BENCH\n    name = os.path.basename(bed).lower()\n    for sp in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"stage_d1_*.json\"))):\n        try:\n            if os.path.basename(str(json.load(open(sp, encoding=\"utf-8\")).get(\"work\") or \"\")).lower() != name:\n                continue\n        except Exception:                                                          # noqa: BLE001\n            continue\n        stage = os.path.basename(sp)[len(\"stage_d1_\"):-len(\".json\")]\n        # cycle-87 firefighter: a simulated stage (docs/stage-simulator-plan.md) keeps its finalized plan under\n        # tools/bench/sim/<stage>/ (plan_<stage>.json, stageplan_<stage>.json), not in tools/bench/; without this\n        # the L2-A1 bed derived 0 licences and every one of its 35 by-design items was `extra` (cycle 87 MISMATCH).\n        cands = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"plan_%s*.json\" % stage)))\n        cands += sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"sim\", stage, \"plan_%s*.json\" % stage)))\n        cands += sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BENCH_, \"sim\", stage, \"stageplan_%s*.json\" % stage)))\n        for pp in cands:\n            try:\n                p = json.load(open(pp, encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            except Exception:                                                      # noqa: BLE001\n                continue\n            if p.get(\"schema\") == \"stageplan/1\" and \"open_rows\" in p:\n                return sp, pp, p\n    return None, None, None\n\n\ndef derive_expected(plan):\n    base = (plan.get(\"base\") or {}).get(\"path\")\n    cls = {}\n    if base and os.path.exists(os.path.join(ROOT, base)):\n        for o in json.load(open(os.path.join(ROOT, base), encoding=\"utf-8\")).get(\"objs\") or []:\n            cls[o.get(\"uid\")] = o.get(\"class\")\n    rules, seen_nodes = [], set()\n    for r in plan.get(\"open_rows\") or []:\n        n, t = int(r[\"node\"]), r[\"term\"]\n        c = cls.get(n)\n        if c == \"SubVI\":\n            rules.append({\"norm_all\": [norm(t), \"isnotwired\"], \"count\": 1, \"required\": False,\n                          \"kind\": \"subvi_input_not_wired\", \"from\": [n, t, c]})\n        elif n not in seen_nodes:\n            rules.append({\"norm_all\": [\"containsunwiredorbadterminal\"], \"count\": 1, \"required\": False,\n                          \"kind\": \"node_unwired\", \"from\": [n, t, c]})\n        seen_nodes.add(n)\n    if plan.get(\"open_rows\"):\n        rules.append({\"norm_any\": list(WIRE_CLASSES), \"count\": None, \"required\": False,\n                      \"kind\": \"wire_from_open_rows\", \"from\": \"all open rows\"})\n    return rules\n\n\ndef _hit(rule, txt):\n    if \"match\" in rule:\n        return rule[\"match\"].lower() in txt.lower()\n    n = norm(txt)\n    if \"norm_all\" in rule:\n        if all(k in n for k in rule[\"norm_all\"]):\n            return True\n        n2 = ocr_fold(n)                                   # card 127-2: OCR-alias fallback (only adds matches)\n        return all(ocr_fold(k) in n2 for k in rule[\"norm_all\"])\n    if any(k in n for k in rule.get(\"norm_any\") or []):\n        return True\n    n2 = ocr_fold(n)\n    return any(ocr_fold(k) in n2 for k in rule.get(\"norm_any\") or [])\n\n\ndef compare(items, expected, derived=()):\n    \"\"\"Explicit expected entries (file) are REQUIRED; plan-derived licences are not. Returns extra raws, missing\n    explicit matches, and per-rule usage.\"\"\"\n    left = [dict(e, count=int(e.get(\"count\", 1)), required=True, kind=\"explicit\") for e in expected]\n    left += [dict(d) for d in derived]\n    used = [0] * len(left)\n    extra = []\n    for it in items:\n        txt = \"%s %s\" % (it.get(\"raw\") or \"\", it.get(\"detail\") or \"\")\n        k = next((i for i, e in enumerate(left) if (e[\"count\"] is None or e[\"count\"] > 0) and _hit(e, txt)), None)\n        if k is None:\n            extra.append(it.get(\"raw\"))\n            continue\n        used[k] += 1\n        it[\"licensed_by\"] = left[k][\"kind\"]\n        if left[k][\"count\"] is not None:\n            left[k][\"count\"] -= 1\n    missing = [e.get(\"match\") for e in left if e[\"required\"] for _ in range(e[\"count\"])]\n    usage = [{\"kind\": e[\"kind\"], \"from\": e.get(\"from\") or e.get(\"match\"), \"used\": u} for e, u in zip(left, used)]\n    heads = license_headers(items)\n    for pos in heads:                                   # remove exactly the licensed empty headers from `extra`\n        extra.remove(items[pos].get(\"raw\"))\n    usage.append({\"kind\": \"header_of_next\", \"from\": \"PD179(d): empty-raw tree header before a licensed item\",\n                  \"used\": len(heads)})\n    return extra, missing, usage\n\n\n# TREE-HEADER ROWS (card 80-4, plan PD179(d), 2026-09-25): the Error List shows a subVI's required-input error as a\n# tree - a header row whose OCR text can come back EMPTY, then the item row. cycle 80 read item 0 raw='' with the\n# detail of item 1 (#5058 'Image In' is not wired, licensed by an open row) and called it extra. An empty-raw row is\n# licensed ONLY when (a) the NEXT item is itself licensed and non-empty, and (b) the header's detail text (the error\n# class description) equals that item's detail after norm(). It consumes no licence count. Anything else stays extra.\n\ndef license_headers(items):\n    \"\"\"Mark `licensed_by = 'header-of <n>'` on qualifying empty-raw rows; return their positions in `items`.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for pos, it in enumerate(items):\n        if it.get(\"licensed_by\") or norm(it.get(\"raw\")) or pos + 1 >= len(items):\n            continue\n        nxt = items[pos + 1]\n        det = norm(it.get(\"detail\"))\n        if not (nxt.get(\"licensed_by\") and not str(nxt[\"licensed_by\"]).startswith(\"header-of\")\n                and norm(nxt.get(\"raw\")) and det and det == norm(nxt.get(\"detail\"))):\n            continue\n        it[\"licensed_by\"] = \"header-of %s\" % nxt.get(\"index\", pos + 1)\n        out.append(pos)\n    return out\n\n\n# COUNT-ONLY SCRATCH READ (card chat-P2 item 3, user 2026-09-28 \"1~4번 적용\"): a stage that reads the Error List of a\n# SCRATCH copy and then of the saved FINAL file paid two full reads (pool stage: scratch 664 s + final 665 s). The\n# expensive part of a full read is the per-item double-click (make_on_item: two block-diagram captures + 1.5 s each).\n# `--count-only --role scratch` walks the list WITHOUT the double-clicks (rows and details are still OCR'd, so every\n# item's text and the per-class counts are read) and compares the per-class counts with the expected file; if they\n# differ (any extra, any missing, or items != the window's own N) the FULL read runs at once on the same scratch,\n# exactly as before. `--role final` (the default) ALWAYS gets the full read: --count-only is refused for it and said so.\ndef class_counts(items, ocr=False):\n    \"\"\"{norm(raw): n} over the read items - the per-class counts a count-only read is judged by. card 127-2: ocr=True\n    keys by norm_ocr (OCR aliases folded, e.g. subvi/subvl one class); the default is unchanged.\"\"\"\n    out = {}\n    for it in items or []:\n        k = norm_ocr(it.get(\"raw\")) if ocr else norm(it.get(\"raw\"))\n        out[k] = out.get(k, 0) + 1\n    return dict(sorted(out.items()))\n\n\ndef count_only_differs(items, n_reported, expected, derived):\n    \"\"\"(differs: bool, why: str) - a count-only read is accepted only when it matches the expectation exactly.\"\"\"\n    import copy\n    ex, mi, _u = compare(copy.deepcopy(items or []), expected, [dict(d) for d in derived])\n    why = []\n    if n_reported is None or len(items or []) != n_reported:\n        why.append(\"items %s != window N %s\" % (len(items or []), n_reported))\n    if ex:\n        why.append(\"%d extra\" % len(ex))","numLines":180,"startLine":310,"totalLines":768}}}
